<title>UK: AHK remains biggest carrier at Manchester in 1996.</title>
<headline>AHK remains biggest carrier at Manchester in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cathay Pacific subsidiary Air Hong Kong held its position as top freight carrier at Manchester airport last year, draft airport statistics show.</p>
<p>Total cargo handled at Manchester last year at 85,101 tonnes was 1.5 percent down on 1995. London Heathrow dominates the other UK airports in terms of tonnage carried and in 1995 Manchester lay fourth in the UK listings behind the three London airports.</p>
<p>The main freight carriers using Manchester last year (imports and exports combined) in tonnes with percentage change from 1995 tonnages are:</p>
<p> AIRLINE	    1996 TONNAGE   PCT CHANGE FROM 95</p>
<p> AIR HONG KONG	 16,447	 DOWN   1.0</p>
<p> BRITISH AIRWAYS     10,157	 DOWN   2.0</p>
<p> AMERICAN AIRWAYS     6,784	 DOWN  14.0</p>
<p> HEAVYLIFT CARGO	5,718	 DOWN  44.0</p>
<p> DELTA AIR LINES	4,482	 DOWN   7.0</p>
<p> CATHAY PACIFIC	 3,599	 DOWN   6.0</p>
<p> SINGAPORE AIRLINES   3,156	   UP  21.0</p>
<p> EMIRATES		 2,823	 DOWN  26.0</p>
<p> AIR TOURS		2,564	   UP  39.0</p>
<p> CONTINENTAL	    2,282	   UP 997.0</p>
<p> AER LINGUS	     2,184	 DOWN  27.0</p>
<p> LUFTHANSA		2,179	   UP  68.0</p>
<p> VIRGIN ATLANTIC	2,141		 N.A.</p>
<p> CARGOLUX		 1,750		 N.A.</p>
<p> OTHERS		  17,525</p>
